+
+METRIC.  The metric here is the production p90/max contract itself -- a
+floor measured in any other currency is the F069 defect class.
+
+RIDGE, NOT A SIMPLE EDGE.  Sweeping the (angle, isotropic-scale) plane at
+fixed gamma shows the worst-case accuracy failure is NOT a monotone
+function of ``eta`` alone: it is concentrated in a narrow, non-monotonic
+angular ridge (observed near angle ~= 1.40-1.42 rad, i.e. ~80-81 degrees,
+for gamma=1.2 -- an off-axis direction distinct from the purely transverse
+90-degree direction, where errors stay small even at comparable eta).
+Along a fixed angle the pass/fail pattern can oscillate with radial scale
+before settling into a clean pass for all larger scale, so a naive
+single-crossing bisection can silently lock onto an early (too low)
+crossing and UNDER-report the true worst eta. This script therefore uses a
+two-stage search -- a coarse global grid to locate the ridge, followed by a
+local high-resolution refinement grid around the coarse peak -- rather than
+bisection, to stay robust to that non-monotonicity.
 
